WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 2: Sports and Health.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.320
Welcome to Unit 2: Sports and Health!

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.620
In this unit, you will explore the exciting
world of sports, fitness, and healthy living.

4
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.820
You will read about how athletes
train, what makes a healthy lifestyle,

5
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.460
and how sports bring communities
together across East Africa and beyond.

6
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.140
Along the way, you will learn powerful new vocabulary,

7
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.020
master an important grammar structure
called the First Conditional,

8
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:35.080
and develop your writing and speaking skills through creative
projects like writing a biography and delivering sports

9
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:35.760
commentary.

10
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.580
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:49.460
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use and
understand 28 new vocabulary words related to science,

12
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.140
the environment, and health.

13
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:57.580
you will also identify and use the first conditional
to talk about possible future events and their results.

14
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:03.360
you will also use unless as an alternative
to if not in conditional sentences.

15
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.200
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:14.700
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: geographic,
originally, imagination, agency, prophet, deteriorate.

17
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:21.200
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.040
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:33.620
The reading sequence includes Sports and Health:
source text 1 and Sports and Health: source text 2.

20
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.080
Read actively.

21
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.480
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

22
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.340
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

23
00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:47.360
The first language focus is What Is the First Conditional?.

24
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.920
The First Conditional is a way of talking about
things that are likely or possible in the future.

25
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.480
We use it when we believe there is a
real chance that something will happen,

26
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.360
and we want to describe what the result will be.

27
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.760
For example: Notice the structure in the model examples,

28
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:08.520
then apply it deliberately in
connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.287
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Sports Interview Role-Play.

30
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.740
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.560
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.080
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.160
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.920
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.300
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.140
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
